{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793607318,"nonce":"uK+6Qmku/AuZZn8WBGTCLMKEZnA=","message":"Changed after the 2026-11-02 document review (design §11 updated to match).\n\nScope additions:\n\n- `/` and `%` are modelled here, including `DivideByZeroException` and `int.MinValue / -1` (`OverflowException`). M4 rejected them \"until M6\", but M6 never listed them. The zero-divisor and `MinValue / -1` generators move to M6's differential tests.\n- `decimal` equality: C# says `1.0m == 1.00m`, but the mantissa+scale model holds two different values. `==` on `decimal`, and on records that contain one, translates to the model's numeric equality (field-wise for records), never to Lean `Eq` on the representation. Otherwise the kernel could accept a theorem that is false in C#.\n- The attribute sidecar gains `@[spec]` lemmas, which `mvcgen`-style VC generation selects specs by. It is regenerated for Std and the effect-monad part of the semantics library in the first step.\n\nExit criterion gains: differential and CLR-agreement generators produce equal `decimal` values with different scales (e.g. `1.0m` vs `1.00m`), for both `==` and record equality.\n\nCheckpoints, in order:\n\n1. Std closure exported, kernel-checked in verified mode, and cross-checked. This is a gate: kernel problems found here are fixed before the rest.\n2. Effect monad (exceptions, null, overflow, `/` and `%`), with CLR-agreement tests.\n3. Minimal `decimal`, with the numeric-equality translation.\n4. VC generation on a method with effects but no external hypotheses.\n5. `[ContractFor]` hypotheses and the `ProcessPayment` theorem.\n6. Assumption reports.","files":null}]}